# Anything the Linux container executes must keep LF endings regardless of the
# checkout platform. core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites these on checkout,
# and a start script with CRLF fails as `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` inside the
# image -- a build that succeeds and a container that never starts.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
